{
  "title": "🎯 The nth Term — Jump Straight to Any Position",
  "hook": "Your AP is 3, 7, 11, 15, ... What's the 100th term? You don't need to write out all 100 terms — there's a formula that takes you directly to any term!",
  "explanation": "<p>The <b>nth term</b> of an AP with first term <b>a</b> and common difference <b>d</b>:</p><div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#E3F2FD,#BBDEFB);border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:1.05rem;text-align:center\"><div style=\"font-size:0.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:#1565C0;margin-bottom:4px\">nth Term Formula</div><strong>aₙ = a + (n − 1)d</strong></div><p>Think of it: start at a, then take (n−1) steps of size d.</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">n</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Formula</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Value for AP: 3, 7, 11, ...</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">1</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">3 + 0(4) = 3</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">2</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">3 + 1(4) = 7</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">7</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">5</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">3 + 4(4) = 19</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">19</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">100</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">3 + 99(4) = 399</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">399</td></tr></table><div style=\"background:#FFF8E1;border-left:4px solid #FFB300;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> You can also use this backwards: if you know a term's value, solve for n to find its position!</div><div style=\"background:#F5F5F5;border-left:3px solid #4A90D9;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 12px;margin:6px 0;font-size:0.9rem\">The nth term formula is <b>linear in n</b>: aₙ = dn + (a−d). If you plot term vs position, you get a straight line!</div>",
  "worked_example": "<b>Example:</b> Find the 20th term of the AP: 2, 7, 12, 17, ...<br><br><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Identify a and d</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">a = 2, d = 7 − 2 = 5</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Apply formula</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">a₂₀ = 2 + (20 − 1) × 5 = 2 + 95 = 97</span></div></div></div><br><b>Example 2:</b> Which term of the AP 5, 13, 21, ... is 181?<br><br><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Set up</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">181 = 5 + (n−1) × 8</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Solve</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">176 = 8(n−1) → n−1 = 22 → n = 23</span></div></div></div><div style=\"background:#F5F5F5;border-left:3px solid #4A90D9;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 12px;margin:6px 0;font-size:0.9rem\">181 is the <b>23rd term</b> of this AP.</div>",
  "try_this": {
    "question": "Find the 15th term of the AP: 10, 6, 2, −2, ...",
    "hint": "a = 10, d = 6 − 10 = −4. Use aₙ = a + (n−1)d.",
    "answer": "a₁₅ = 10 + 14 × (−4) = 10 − 56 = −46."
  },
  "fun_fact": "The concept of going 'straight to the nth term' is the heart of random access in computers — just like how a computer can jump to any memory address, you can jump to any term in an AP!"
}